Actually wait — the 500 is happening now, "since yesterday's merge." The merge is FLOW-226 (audit before decrypt on read) and SEC-52 (throw if read can't be audited). Before FLOW-226, the GET route probably didn't call auditAccess at all. So the read path is new, and audit.ts was changed so that a failed audit write throws on read. So if the audit write fails on the dev stack (e.g., the AuditLog table doesn't exist in the shared DB, or a prisma migration is missing), the read throws → 500.

But wait, the create/update/delete routes also call auditAccess. So if the AuditLog table didn't exist, those should also have been failing. Unless… those were working before. Hmm.

Let me check the git history of audit.ts and the schema. Let me also look at the test files.

